  [1m[4mSUPABASE[24m[22m [2m(3)[22m

  [1m[41m[37m CRITICAL [39m[49m[22m [1mTable "todos" has Row Level Security disabled[22m  [2msupabase/rls-disabled[22m
             [36msupabase/migrations/20240115120000_init.sql:17[39m
             [2m│[22m [90mcreate table public.todos ([39m
             public.todos is created without `enable row level security` in any migration; the table
             is readable and writable with the public anon key.
             [32mFix [39m Add `alter table <name> enable row level security;` in a new migration, then write
                  policies scoped to the owner, e.g. `create policy "own rows" on <name> for all
                  using (auth.uid() = user_id) with check (auth.uid() = user_id);`.

  [1m[41m[37m CRITICAL [39m[49m[22m [1mSupabase service_role key used in browser code[22m  [2msupabase/service-role-in-client[22m
             [36mlib/supabase.ts:5[39m
             [2m│[22m [90mconst supabaseKey = process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY!;[39m
             lib/supabase.ts is part of the browser bundle (imported via app/dashboard/page.tsx) and
             reads NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY.
             [32mFix [39m Create the admin client in a server-only module (`import "server-only"` at the top
                  of lib/supabase/admin.ts) and use it exclusively from route handlers / server
                  actions after checking the user. In the browser use the anon key with RLS
                  policies.

  [1m[43m[30m HIGH     [39m[49m[22m [1mPolicy "Enable all access for all users" lets anyone with[22m  [2msupabase/permissive-policy[22m
             [1myour public anon key write "notes"[22m
             [36msupabase/migrations/20240115120000_init.sql:35[39m
             [2m│[22m [90mcreate policy "Enable all access for all users"[39m
             Policy "Enable all access for all users" on public.notes (FOR ALL, TO public) uses
             `true`: anyone with your public anon key can read, insert, update and delete every row
             of notes.
             [32mFix [39m Scope the policy to the row owner, e.g. `using (auth.uid() = user_id)` and `with
                  check (auth.uid() = user_id)`. Keep `true` only for SELECT on genuinely public
                  data (e.g. published blog posts) and say so in a comment.

  [1m[4mAPPLICATION SECURITY[24m[22m [2m(11)[22m

  [1m[41m[37m CRITICAL [39m[49m[22m [1mWebhook trusts unsigned requests[22m  [2msecurity/unverified-webhook[22m[2m ~heuristic[22m
             [36mapp/api/webhooks/stripe/route.ts:4[39m
             [2m│[22m [90mexport async function POST(req: Request) {[39m
             app/api/webhooks/stripe/route.ts handles webhook events (Stripe payment events) but
             never verifies the provider signature.
             [32mFix [39m Verify the signature with the raw body before parsing: for Stripe,
                  `stripe.webhooks.constructEvent(await req.text(),
                  req.headers.get("stripe-signature"), process.env.STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET)`. For
                  other providers use their SDK verifier (svix, @octokit/webhooks) or an HMAC with
                  timingSafeEqual.

