                  default-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data: https:; connect-src 'self'
                  https://<project>.supabase.co; frame-ancestors 'none'`. For Next.js with inline
                  scripts, use the nonce-based middleware pattern from the Next.js CSP guide.

  [1m[44m[37m MEDIUM   [39m[49m[22m [1m5 of 5 recommended security headers missing[22m  [2msecurity/missing-security-headers[22m
             [36mnext.config.js[39m
             No configuration sets: Strict-Transport-Security (forces HTTPS); X-Frame-Options /
             frame-ancestors (prevents clickjacking); X-Content-Type-Options (stops MIME sniffing);
             Referrer-Policy (limits URL leakage to third parties); Permissions-Policy (disables
             unused browser features).
             [32mFix [39m Add an `async headers()` block to next.config (or `headers` in vercel.json /
                  `_headers` on Netlify / `helmet()` in Express) that sets
                  Strict-Transport-Security, X-Frame-Options: DENY, X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff,
                  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin and Permissions-Policy.

